The part about randomly generated:

Certain monsters come with equipment that is standard for them.
It's still based on chances, but assorted monsters come with
chances of armor or weapons.  Some like soldiers might carry food.
Minotaurs might have a /WoDig.  Tools like bugle, pickaxe and
mirror can get created with monsters.  But no monster ever gets a
magic whistle in their regular assortment of equipment.  That
still leaves randomly generated objects.  On the floor, in shops,
and in a monsters inventory when the monster is created.  This
combination of randomly-determined items from a standard catalog
plus randomly-generated random items skews the loot that builds
up in your hoard toward the catalog items.  You get a lot of
orcish weapons and armor killing orcs, a lot of weapon and armor
fighting soldiers, etc.  But to get a magic whistle you have to
encounter many randomly generated items.

